.TH SWAYDESK-GREETER 1 2026-11-15 "swaydesk 0.1.3.1" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-greeter \- login screen for greetd, in the look of the Sway desktop lock screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-greeter
.SH DESCRIPTION
A graphical login screen in GTK 4. greetd starts it inside a Sway of its own, with no key bindings and no
Xwayland, through
.IR /usr/share/swaydesk\-greeter/sway.conf ;
the package's drop-in for greetd.service makes greetd read
.I /usr/share/swaydesk\-greeter/greetd.toml
instead of
.IR /etc/greetd/config.toml .
.PP
It lists the people's accounts (UID between UID_MIN and UID_MAX of
.IR /etc/login.defs ,
with a login shell) with their AccountsService photo, plus "Other user\&...". The password answers PAM's first
question; any further question (a code, an expired password) appears in the same field, one at a time. The
session list comes from the wayland\-sessions directories of XDG_DATA_DIRS, with Sway Desktop first. The last
account and each account's session are remembered. It uses the system keyboard layout, language and session
cursor, and has suspend, restart and shut down buttons.
.PP
It takes no arguments and exits with 2 when given any.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GREETD_SOCK
The greetd socket, set by greetd.
.TP
.B SWAYDESK_GREETER_CONFIG, SWAYDESK_GREETER_STATE
Replace the configuration and the memory file; for tests only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/swaydesk\-greeter/config.toml
Optional: accent (\fBaccent = "#8e44ad"\fR) and language (\fBlocale = "pt_BR"\fR), in the format of the user's
config.toml.
.TP
.I /etc/swaydesk\-greeter/sway.d/*.conf
Sway commands for this machine's login screen (outputs, scale).
.TP
.I /var/lib/swaydesk\-greeter/state.json
The last account and session, written only by the greeter user (the directory is 0700).
.TP
.I /var/lib/AccountsService/icons/<login>
The account photo: PNG or JPEG, up to 2 MiB and 2048x2048.
.TP
.I /etc/default/keyboard, /etc/locale.conf, /etc/default/locale
The system keyboard and language. For the keyboard, /etc/default/keyboard or systemd's
/etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/00-keyboard.conf or /etc/vconsole.conf, whichever changed last.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/swaydesk\-greeter
The PAM service of the sessions opened from the login screen (greetd.toml's
.BR [general] " service" ).
On Debian and Ubuntu it is the login stack, with the system language from /etc/default/locale, plus
gnome\-keyring, which unlocks the login keyring with the login password; on Arch, system\-local\-login plus
gnome\-keyring. The login screen's own session keeps greetd's service.
Changes to the PAM of the logins from this screen (a fingerprint reader, a security key) go in this file, not in
.IR /etc/pam.d/greetd ;
what pam\-auth\-update puts in common\-auth applies to both.
.SH NOTES
To go back to the greeter of /etc/greetd/config.toml without removing the package:
.PP
.nf
mkdir \-p /etc/systemd/system/greetd.service.d
ln \-s /dev/null /etc/systemd/system/greetd.service.d/swaydesk\-greeter.conf
systemctl daemon\-reload
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR greetd (1),
.BR greetd (5),
.BR sway (1),
.BR swaydesk (7)
